index 0000000..6806934
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/workflows/pod-base.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,263 @@
+name: pod-base
+
+# The dev-pod toolchain base image (`engine/Dockerfile.pod`).
+#
+# Why this workflow exists, in one measurement: on the `dev` build of
+# 2026-08-18 the merged image took 34 minutes, and 1344s of that — 22 minutes —
+# was installing a toolchain that no commit in this repository had touched.
+# apt, rustup, five `cargo install`s, sway, GStreamer, the JDK, Gradle, the
+# Android SDK, Flutter. It was rebuilt every push because it lived in the same
+# Dockerfile as the product, and because nothing was cached between runs.
+#
+# So it is built here instead, published, and consumed by digest. An ordinary
+# push now *pulls* the toolchain rather than building it.
+#
+# ── Tagging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+#
+#   <variant>-<hash>-<week>      e.g. full-9f3c1a7b2e40-2026W34
+#
+# `<hash>` is a digest of `engine/Dockerfile.pod`, so editing that file
+# produces a new tag on the next build and the old one stays exactly as it
+# was. `<week>` is the ISO week, so an unchanged file is still rebuilt once a
+# week — which is load-bearing rather than tidy-minded: `rclone`, `sccache`,
+# `gh`, `step`, `github-mcp-server`, Gradle and `selkies` all resolve *latest*
+# at build time, and a purely content-addressed tag would have frozen every
+# one of them at whatever the first build happened to see while looking like
+# reproducibility.
+#
+# A build is skipped entirely when its tag already exists in GHCR — the same
+# shape as `mirror-base-images.yml`, and for the same reason: this runs as a
+# prerequisite of every image build, so the common case has to be a lookup.
+#
+# ── What this is not ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+#
+# It is not in the `vogt-base/` namespace, deliberately. That prefix means
+# "a verbatim mirror of an upstream library image" and `mirror-base-images.yml`
+# greps the Dockerfiles for it to decide what to copy from Docker Hub. This
+# image is built here and has no upstream, so it is `vogt-pod-base` and the
+# mirror correctly ignores it. `engine/Dockerfile.pod`'s own `FROM` still names
+# a mirrored base, and that file is now in the mirror's file list.
+#
+# It is also not deployed. Nothing here reaches Node B: the image lives in
+# GHCR, `build.yml` consumes it by digest, and production still moves only when
+# the digest pinned in `indexarr/ops` changes and Komodo runs `DeployStack`
+# (NFR-D10). This workflow adds no infrastructure to the estate.
+
+on:
+  workflow_call:
+    inputs:
+      variant:
+        description: lean (no Flutter — main and releases) or full (dev)
+        required: true
+        type: string
+    outputs:
+      image:
+        description: The pod base, by digest, for POD_BASE_IMAGE
